title: Cornered — the exit obeys the world, the thread survives it
story: ides-of-march
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: The poet's jest answer ends with him quitting the scene —
  legal while the tiring-house door can be opened. His walking out
  parks the book conversation where it stood; the next ask picks it
  back up. The locked-door half of the old scenario lives in
  cornered-locked.transcript, which needs the question still unasked.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/ides-of-march/chord/ides-of-march.story
    stories/ides-of-march/tests/transcripts/cornered.transcript

---

> north
[OK: contains "Stage"]

> west
[OK: contains "Tiring-House"]

> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "The new hired man"]

# Fresh scene, first topic: the plain book row, question on its heels.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "So it is not carried"]

# The jest answer serves and he quits the scene — the exit is legal.
> ask shakespeare about a spy
[OK: contains "given in jest"]

# His exit closed the scene, and the close parked the book talk where
# it stood — the next ask picks it up, not the beginning.
> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "You wear a path"]

> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "You always come back to it"]
